                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Either of two units of measure of the calculating speed of a computer:",
                                            "a quadrillion (10¹⁵) floating point operations per second."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e18656a1-5fa0-4b49-bb6b-c839667ca922",
                                                "sense_id": "3dfa55a6-92ca-38bf-aa8d-a6f32a32a369",
                                                "text": "...a better machine is a petaflop machine. A petaflop is a quadrillion flops, a quadrillion floating-point operations per second, so a petaflop machine is a thousand times as fast as a teraflop machine, or a million times as fast as a Cray Y-MP8. The petaflop machine will exist by the year 2000, or soon afterward."
                                            }
                                        ]
